          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            The concept of a
            %em smooth sets
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %em smooth spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Schreiber13"} Schreiber 2013
            = succeed "&rbrack;," do
              %a{:href => "#Schreiber14"} 2014
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            beyond that of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+space"} generalized smooth space
            that is characterized by how it may be
            %em probed
            by smooth
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
          %p
            For example,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces"} moduli spaces
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
            exist as smooth sets but not as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
            (much less as
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics"} geometry of physics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+calculus"} variational calculus
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#Schreiber13b"}> Schreiber 2013b
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Schreiber17"} 2017
            = succeed "&rbrack;." do
              %a{:href => "#GiotopoulosSati23"} Giotopoulos &amp; Sati 2023
          %p
            Hence the category of smooth sets is a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nice+category+of+spaces"} convenient categories of spaces
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+topology"} differential topology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            and in fact a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive topos
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#Schreiber13"}> Schreiber 2013 §4.4
            \&amp;rbrack;.
          %p
            From a broader perspective, smooth sets are equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+truncation"} 0-truncated
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} smooth ∞-groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"}
              cohesive
              = succeed "-topos" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            (exposition in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Schreiber25"} Schreiber 2025
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nice+category+of+spaces"} convenient categories of spaces
            for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+topology"} differential topology
          %div{:style => "margin: -20px 0px 20px 20px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/ConvenientCategoriesOfSpaces.png", :width => "860px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                From
                %a{:href => "#SatiSchreiber25"} Sati-Schreiber 2025
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            One way to define category of
            %strong smooth sets
            is as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SmthSet
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi SmthMfd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  SmthSet
                  \\coloneqq
                  Sh(SmthMfd)
          %p
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmthMfd"} SmthMfd
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            equipped with its standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"}> Grothendieck topology
            ) given by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+covers"} open covers
          %p
            Since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SmthMfd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SmthMfd
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
            to the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            %em embedded
            into
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^\infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SmthMfd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SmthMfd
            is an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+small+category"} essentially small category
          %p
            But since manifolds themselves are defined in terms of gluing conditons, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SmthSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SmthSet
            depends on much less than all of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SmthMfd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SmthMfd
          %p Let
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ball
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi D
                    %mi int
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi D
                    %mi int
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi SmthMfd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi m
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Ball
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\big\{
                  (D^n_{int}
                  \\to
                  D^m_{int})
                  \\in SmthMfd
                  \\vert
                  n,m \in \mathbb{N}
                  \\big\}
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CartSp
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi SmthMfd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi m
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CartSp
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\big\{
                  (\mathbb{R}^n
                  \\to
                  \\mathbb{R}^m)
                  \\in SmthMfd
                  \\vert|
                  n,m \in \mathbb{N}
                  \\big\}
          %p
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategories"} full subcategories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ball
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ball
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SmthMfd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SmthMfd
            on open balls and on cartesian spaces, respectively. Then the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toposes"} toposes
            are still those of smooth spaces:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi SmthSet
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi Sh
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Ball
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi Sh
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi CartSp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  SmthSet
                  \&amp;\simeq Sh(Ball)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \simeq Sh(CartSp)
                  \\end{aligned}
                  \\,.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The category of ordinary
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
                of smooth spaces:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SmthMfd
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi SmoothSet
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      SmthMfd \hookrightarrow SmoothSet
                      \\,.
              %p
                When one regards smooth spaces concretely as sheaves on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SmthMfd
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SmthMfd
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            %li
              %p
                The full
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi DiffSp
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi SmoothSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      DiffSp \subset SmoothSet
              %p
                on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+sheaf"} concrete sheaves
                is called the category of
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    The standard class of examples of smooth spaces that motivate their use even in cases where one starts out being intersted just in
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
                    are
                    = succeed ":" do
                      %strong mapping spaces
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                    and
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Σ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                    two smooth spaces (possibly just ordinary smooth manifolds), by the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+structure+on+presheaves"} closed monoidal structure on presheaves
                    the
                    %strong mapping space
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi Σ
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma,X]
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo →
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \to X
                    exists again naturally as a smooth. By the general formula it is given as a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
                    by the assignment
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mi U
                          %mo ↦
                          %mi SmthSet
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo ×
                          %mi U
                          %mo ,
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo .
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          [\Sigma,X]
                          \\colon
                          U \mapsto SmthSet(\Sigma \times U, X)
                          \\,.
                  %p
                    If
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                    and
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Σ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                    are ordinary manifolds, then the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
                    on the right sits inside that of the underlying sets
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi SmthSet
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo ×
                          %mi U
                          %mo ,
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mi Set
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi Σ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mo ×
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mo ,
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SmthSet(\Sigma \times U , X) \subset Set({|\Sigma|} \times {|U|}, {|X|} )
                    so that
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma,X]
                    is a
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+space"} diffeological space
                  %p
                    The above formula says that a
                    = succeed "-parameterized" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi U
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo →
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \to X
                    is smooth as a map into the smooth space
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma,X ]
                    precisely if the corresponding map of sets
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                          %mo ×
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo →
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \times \Sigma \to X
                    is an ordinary morphism of smooth manifolds.
            %li
              %p
                The canonical examples of smooth spaces that are not diffeological spaces are the sheaves of (closed)
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi K
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi U
                      %mo ↦
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi closed
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      K^n \colon U \mapsto \Omega^n_{closed}(U)
                      \\,.
            %li
              %p The category
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SimpSmthSet
                      %mo ≔
                      %msup
                        %mi SmthSet
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      SimpSmthSet
                      \\coloneqq
                      SmthSet^{\Delta^{op}}
              %p
                equivalently that of sheaves on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SmthMfd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SmthMfd
                with values in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi SmthMfd
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\cdots \simeq Sh(SmthMfd, sSet)
              %p
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects"} simplicial objects
                in smooth spaces naturally carries the structure of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+category"} homotopical category
                (for instance the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sheaves"} model structure on simplicial sheaves
                or that of a Brown
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
                (if one restricts to locally Kan simplicial sheaves)) and as such is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentation
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-stacks"}> smooth ∞-stacks
                \.
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %h3#Cohesion Cohesion
          #SmoothSetsFormACohesiveTopos.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
                form a
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive topos
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SmoothSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SmoothSet
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive topos
            #eq:SheafToposAdjointQuadruple.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SmoothSet
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AAA
                                %msub
                                  %mi Π
                                  %mn 0
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AAA
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟵
                              %mrow
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AA
                                %mi Disc
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AA
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AAA
                                %mi Γ
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AAA
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟵
                              %mrow
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AA
                                %mi coDisc
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AA
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    SmoothSet
                    \\array{
                    \\overset{\phantom{AAA} \Pi_0 \phantom{AAA}}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\\
                    \\overset{\phantom{AA} Disc \phantom{AA} }{\longleftarrow}
                    \\\
                    \\overset{\phantom{AAA} \Gamma \phantom{AAA} }{\longrightarrow}
                    \\\
                    \\overset{\phantom{AA} coDisc \phantom{AA} }{\longleftarrow}
                    }
                    Set
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              First of all (by
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+smooth+sets#CategoryOfSmoothSets"} this Prop
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              between them, and equipped with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
              of differentiably-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+covers"} good open covers
              (
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+smooth+sets#DifferentiallyGoodOpenCover"}> this def.
              )
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SmoothSet
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    SmoothSet \simeq Sh(CartSp)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence, by Prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoriesOfSheavesOnCohesiveSiteIsCohesive"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+site"} cohesive site
              (Def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OneCohesiveSite"}
            %p
              It clearly has
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+products"} finite products
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              is the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\ast = \mathbb{R}^0
            %p
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              of two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
              is the Cartesian space whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum"} sum
              of the two separate dimensions:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^{n_1} \times \mathbb{R}^{n_2}
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\mathbb{R}^{ n_1 + n_2 }
                    \\,.
            %p
              This establishes the first clause in Def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OneCohesiveSite"}
            %p
              For the second clause, consider a differentiably-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+cover"} good open cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \overset{}{\to} \mathbb{R}^n\}
              (
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+smooth+sets#DifferentiallyGoodOpenCover"}> this def.
              ). This being a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+cover"} good cover
              implies that its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+groupoid"} Cech groupoid
              is, as an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+groupoid"} internal groupoid
              (via
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#PresheavesOfGroupoidsAsInternalGroupoidsInPresheaves"} this remark
            #eq:CechGroupoidForCartSp.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %munder
                                %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                                %mrow
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi j
                              %mi y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi U
                                %mi i
                              %munder
                                %mo ∩
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi ℝ
                                    %mi n
                              %msub
                                %mi U
                                %mi j
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↑
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
