            %p
              Here we first used that
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits+commute+with+colimits"} colimits commute with colimits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
              (
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#LimitsCommuteWithLimits"}> this prop.
              ) and then that the colimit of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+presheaf"} representable presheaf
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
              set (
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#ColimitOfRepresentableIsSingleton"}> this Lemma
              ).
            %p
              This colimiting
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph"} graph
              carries a unique
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              structure making it a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            %p
              Precisely this operation on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+groupoids"} Cech groupoids
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+covers"} good open covers
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              is what
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borsuk%27s+nerve+theorem"} Borsuk's nerve theorem
              is about, a classical result in
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
              of the groupoid
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ColimitOfCechGroupoidOverCartSp"} (4)
              is in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
              with the set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected topological space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi CartSp
                            %mi op
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_0
                    \\underset{\underset{CartSp^{op}}{\longrightarrow}}{\lim}
                    C(\{U_i\}_i)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\ast
                    \\,.
            %p
              The second item of the second clause in Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OneCohesiveSite"}
              follows similarly, but more easily: The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+groupoid"} Cech groupoid
              is readily seen to be, as before, the unique groupoid structure on the limiting underlying graph of presheaves. Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast = \mathbb{R}^0
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi CartSp
                        %mi op
