          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The category of sheaves of the site of smooth manifolds is considered as a model for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
            inL
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
              , Ch. 6 in:
              %em Faisceaux localement asphériques
              (2003) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://cisinski.app.uni-regensburg.de/mtest2.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Cisinski-FaisceauxLocAsph.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy+theory"} simplicial homotopy theory
            in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Dugger"}> Daniel Dugger
              , section 3.4, from page 29 on in:
              %em Sheaves and Homotopy Theory
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.uoregon.edu/~ddugger/cech.html"}> web
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/cech.pdf"} pdf
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} topos points
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Diff
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(Diff)
                  are discussed there in example 4.1.2 on p. 36, mentioned before on p. 31)
          %p
            and as a model for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+spaces"} generalized smooth spaces
            in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ib+Madsen"}> Ib Madsen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Weiss"} Michael Weiss
              = succeed "," do
                %em The stable moduli space of Riemann surfaces: Mumford’s conjecture
              %strong 165
              3 (2007) 843–941 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0212321"}> arXiv:math/0212321
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/http://doi.org/10.4007/annals.2007.165.843"} doi:10.4007/annals.2007.165.843
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (where a special case of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+Oka+principle"} smooth Oka principle
                  is proven)
          %p
            The equivalent incarnation over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+subsite"} dense subsite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
            and the understanding as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive topos
            is due to:
          %ul
            %li#Schreiber13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              , Def. 1.2.16, Def. 1.3.58 of:
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1310.7930"}> arXiv:1310.7930
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p#TerminologyOrigin The terminology “smooth set” is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                nLab:
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+set"} smooth set
                — from
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/smooth+set/10"} revision 10
                on (Feb 2013)
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#Schreiber13"}> Schreiber 2013
                ,
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1310.7930v1#page=48"} §1.2.2, p. 48
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (which otherwise speaks of “smooth
                  = succeed "\u201D)" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-types"} 0-types
            %li#Schreiber14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                \:
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+smooth+sets"} geometry of physics – smooth sets
                — from
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/geometry+of+physics+--+smooth+sets/3"} revision 3
                on (Nov 2014)
            %li#KhavkineSchreiber17
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Khavkine"}> Igor Khavkine
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Synthetic+variational+calculus"} Synthetic geometry of differential equations: I. Jets and comonad structure
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1701.06238"}> arXiv:1701.06238
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (generalization to
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+smooth+sets"} formal smooth sets
          %p
            further discussed in the context of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28infinity%2C1%29-toposes"}> higher
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+cohesion"} singular
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+toposes"} cohesive toposes
            in:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+Character+Map+in+Non-Abelian+Cohomology"} The Character Map in Non-Abelian Cohomology
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/13422"} doi:10.1142/13422
            %li#SatiSchreiber25
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Equivariant+Principal+infinity-Bundles"}
                      Equivariant Principal
                      = succeed "-Bundles" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mn ∞
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.13654"} arXiv:2112.13654
          %p
            Discussion of smooth sets as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convenient+category+of+spaces"} convenient category
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+calculus"} variational calculus
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+quantum+field+theory"} Lagrangian
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theory"} classical field theory
          %ul
            %li#Schreiber13b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                \:
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Classical+field+theory+via+Cohesive+homotopy+types"} Classical field theory via Cohesive homotopy types
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1311.1172"}> arXiv:1311.1172
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "/schreiber/files/classicalinhigher.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Schreiber17
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} Geometry of Physics – Perturbative Quantum Field Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/65-409%3A+Mathematical+Quantum+Field+Theory"} Mathematical Quantum Field Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Schreiber_pQFT20211103.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.physicsforums.com/insights/a-first-idea-of-quantum-field-theory/"} PhysicsForums version
            %li#GiotopoulosSati23
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grigorios+Giotopoulos"}> Grigorios Giotopoulos
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
